FG-K0-08599e05a7 || cls=MX mod=MUST dom=MX rel=PE pol=GOV-017~ conf=M || actor=agent; act=product inputs never silently override file, register or standard; deviation from a default needs a reason and must be reported; trig=always; scope=root CLAUDE.md; exc=may request a change; time=always; enf=text || test=Precedence is topology and approval routing. Reporting a deviation is a non-entailed extra under C7. The reported worry, constraining authorized spec choices, is real: GOV-001 makes the spec authoritative on product behavior, but this line limits itself to not overriding policy silently.
FG-K0-0f7b627b11 || cls=CO mod=MUST dom=PE rel=FE pol=DEP-007~ conf=M || actor=agent; act=keep package.json and lock in version control and consistent; trig=npm dependency change; scope=dependencies rule, path scoped; exc=none; time=with change; enf=text || test=Commit here says what belongs in version control, not when to run git commit. So no conflict with GOV-015: a lockfile is committed when a commit is requested. Reported tension does not hold.
FG-K0-172287a31c || cls=CO mod=MUST dom=WF rel=FE pol=WF-014~,WF-008~ conf=M || actor=agent; act=bounded iteration; stop and reassess on listed conditions; trig=build-fix loop; scope=build-fix skill; exc=none; time=repair; enf=text || test=Bounded iteration matches WF-014. Stop and reassess is not halt: the reported worry over stopping possible repair overreads it. Listed conditions flesh out genuine user input in WF-008.
